1
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:09,000
Based on a true story.

2
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:12,000
Out of Africa is a history, romance, drama film directed by Sydney Pollack.

3
00:24:09,000 --> 00:24:15,000
Tells the life story of Danish author Karen Blixen, who at the beginning of the
20th century moved to Africa to build a new life for herself.

4
00:32:12,000 --> 00:32:18,000
The film is based on her 1937 autobiographical novel.

5
00:40:15,000 --> 00:40:21,000
Denys George Finch Hatton, played by Robert Redford.

6
00:48:18,000 --> 00:48:24,000
Karen Christence Dinesen Blixen, played by Meryl Streep.

7
00:56:21,000 --> 00:56:27,000
Baron Bror Blixen/Baron Hans Blixen, played by Klaus Maria Brandauer.

8
01:04:24,000 --> 01:04:30,000
Berkeley Cole, played by Michael Kitchen.

9
01:12:27,000 --> 01:12:33,000
Farah, played by Malick Bowens.

10
01:20:30,000 --> 01:20:36,000
Lord Delamere, played by Michael Gough.

11
01:28:33,000 --> 01:28:39,000
Out of Africa is a 1985 American epic romantic drama film directed and produced
by Sydney Pollack, and starring Meryl Streep and Robert Redford.

12
01:36:36,000 --> 01:36:42,000
The film is based loosely on the 1937 autobiographical book Out of Africa written by Isak Dinesen (the pseudonym of Danish
author Karen Blixen), with additional material from Dinesen's 1960 book Shadows on the Grass and other sources.

13
01:44:39,000 --> 01:44:45,000
The book was adapted into a screenplay by Kurt Luedtke,
and this screenplay was filmed in 1984.

14
01:52:42,000 --> 01:52:48,000
Streep played Karen Blixen, Redford played Denys Finch Hatton, and
Klaus Maria Brandauer played Baron Bror Blixen.

15
02:00:45,000 --> 02:00:51,000
Others in the film include Michael Kitchen as Berkeley Cole, Malick Bowens as Farah, Stephen Kinyanjui as the Chief,
Michael Gough as Lord Delamere, Suzanna Hamilton as Felicity, and the model and actress Iman as Mariammo.

16
02:08:48,000 --> 02:08:54,000
The film received generally positive reviews from critics.

17
02:16:51,000 --> 02:16:57,000
It was also a commercial success and won seven Academy Awards
including Best Picture and Best Director for Pollack.

18
02:24:54,000 --> 02:25:00,000
The film explores themes of farm, infidelity, africa, plantation, safari.

19
02:32:57,000 --> 02:33:03,000
The tone is emotional.
